            "role": "assistant",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "“Weather history” can mean either (1) **past daily observations** (what actually happened on specific dates) or (2) **climate normals/averages** (what’s typical). Here are the best ways to get both for **London, Ohio (43140)**:\n\n## 1) Past daily weather (yesterday / last weeks / specific dates)\n- **Timeanddate – Past Weather in London, Ohio**: lets you pick a month and see day-by-day observed highs/lows and conditions (based on a nearby official station).【5:0†source】\n- **Weather Underground – History**: daily/weekly/monthly history view with temperature, precipitation, wind, etc. (station-based).【5:2†source】\n\n## 2) Long-term historical/climatology (year → month → day drilldowns)\n- **WeatherSpark – Weather History in London, Ohio**: jump-off page that lets you drill down by year/month and uses nearby stations (METAR/NOAA ISD) for longer history coverage.【5:3†source】\n\n## 3) Monthly/annual “typical” averages (climate)\n- **43140 London, OH weather averages** (monthly typical highs/lows and rainfall averages).【5:4†source】\n\nIf you tell me **what date range** you want (e.g., “June 2024” or “last 10 years”) and whether you prefer **observed daily data** or **averages**, I can summarize the key numbers (high/low temps, precip, notable extremes) for that period.",
                "annotations": [
                  {
                    "type": "url_citation",
                    "url": "https://www.timeanddate.com/weather/@4517009/historic",
